    description: "FOUND while fixing WI-gabuv (owner_ancestry, finalize sub-step 7d).\n\nSTATEMENT. Spring Data repositories are the Java/Kotlin analogue of `use Ecto.Repo`: `interface UserRepo extends JpaRepository<User, Long>` called as `userRepo.findAll()` / `userRepo.save(u)`. Since WI-gabuv the call edge carries `external_owner_ancestors: [\"JpaRepository\"]` (verified on a fixture: `java:external:0-0:findAll:external_symbol`, receiver_type_hint UserRepo), but no shipped catalogue has a `JpaRepository` / `CrudRepository` / `PagingAndSortingRepository` / `ListCrudRepository` row (java.yaml and kotlin.yaml carry only jakarta/javax.persistence EntityManager + TypedQuery and java.sql), so the calls stay `external_potential`. spring-petclinic: 0 boundary change before/after WI-gabuv for exactly this reason.\n\nAlso observed: the inherited-calls linker's Site-2 Step-3 fallback supersedes the stub with a `calls` edge to the `UserRepo` INTERFACE symbol itself (evidence ast_call_inherited_method), which is not a definition of `findAll`. The io classification is unaffected (the ancestor retry is module-keyed, not the short-name arm), but the resolved edge points at a type, not a member.\n\nFIX DIRECTION. A community overlay (provenance: community, like python-web-and-orm.yaml) with db_read rows (findAll, findById, findAllById, existsById, count, getReferenceById?, findBy* is derived-query and NOT a fixed name) and db_write rows (save, saveAll, saveAndFlush, delete*, deleteAll*, flush) for org.springframework.data.repository.CrudRepository / ListCrudRepository / PagingAndSortingRepository and org.springframework.data.jpa.repository.JpaRepository, cited to the Spring Data source. Check that the unqualified parent name `JpaRepository` (the java analyzer does not qualify an external base through imports, WI-pivap) matches the qualified row module by the component rule. Derived query methods declared on the user interface (`findByName`) are OWN members by owner_ancestry's rule and need a separate decision."  # ce15
    fields: {}  # ce15
